If this norm-based governance, which is decentralized and unconsciously created, doesn't seem to capture what we mean by a “monopoly authority” (even though it's the only source of social rule creation and enforcement that exists and, moreover, that enforcement is violent), consider another example.
 Suppose an organized crime family uses threats of violence to run its neighborhood in some country where a state officially exists but pays scant attention to its duties, leaving the neighborhood's inhabitants to their own devices.
 Is the crime family a government?
